TotalSegmentator - craniofacial_structures model
================================================

This directory contains a redistributed copy of a pretrained model from the
TotalSegmentator project. It is NOT an Arterial model, and it is NOT covered by
the CC BY-NC 4.0 licence that applies to the Arterial model weights.

  Upstream project  https://github.com/wasserth/TotalSegmentator
  Copyright         The TotalSegmentator authors
                    (J. Wasserthal et al., University Hospital Basel)
  Licence           Apache License, Version 2.0 - see the LICENSE file
                    next to this notice
  Task              craniofacial_structures (nnU-Net Dataset115_mandible)
  Configuration     nnUNetTrainer_DASegOrd0_NoMirroring__nnUNetPlans__3d_fullres
                    resampled to 0.5 x 0.5 x 0.5 mm
  Classes           1 mandible, 2 teeth_lower, 3 skull, 4 head,
                    5 sinus_maxillary, 6 sinus_frontal, 7 teeth_upper

TotalSegmentator distributes its models in two groups: openly available models
under Apache-2.0, and models that require a licence key from the authors. The
craniofacial_structures task belongs to the openly available Apache-2.0 group
(it is absent from the `commercial_models` map in TotalSegmentator's
`map_to_binary.py`), which is why it can be redistributed here.


Contents
--------

What this directory holds depends on where you obtained it:

  * with the Arterial model weights (the Zenodo archive):
    the nnU-Net metadata (`plans.json`, `dataset.json`) and fold 0 of the
    trained model (`fold_0/checkpoint_final.pth`);
  * in the Arterial source repository on GitHub: the same metadata plus the
    upstream training fingerprint and logs (`dataset_fingerprint.json`,
    `fold_0/debug.json`, `fold_0/progress.png`). The checkpoint is not under
    version control there; it arrives with the weights download.


Changes made in this redistribution
-----------------------------------

The files are the upstream files. Nothing was retrained, fine-tuned or
converted, and no values were edited. The packaging differs:

  * the directory is named `totalsegmentator_mandible/` rather than following
    the upstream nnU-Net dataset naming, so that Arterial can hand it straight
    to `nnUNetPredictor.initialize_from_trained_model_folder`;
  * only fold 0 of the trained model is included;
  * TotalSegmentator's own pre- and post-processing (cropping to the skull,
    resampling, class remapping) is not included. Arterial calls nnU-Net
    directly and uses only class 3 (skull), to split a head-and-neck CTA into
    its head and neck parts before vessel segmentation.

